  "preamble": "The voiceless retroflex (apical postalveolar) affricate [ʈʂ] loses its retroflex (apical, tongue-curled) articulation and is realized as a laminal palato-alveolar affricate [tʃ]. In Croatian and Bosnian this goes together with a merger of the č–ć contrast into a single [tʃ]. The shift is phonetic and regional rather than a widespread historical change. In Quechuan, Proto-Quechuan *ʈʂ merged with *tʃ in most of Quechua II and in Huaylas and Huánuco Quechua (*ʈʂunka > ʧuŋka 'ten'); Huanca, Pacaraos and Cajamarca keep the retroflex.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deretroflexion, Merger",
